# Canary patterns for script/guard_repo.sh — copy to `.canary` (gitignored).
#
# One extended regex per line. If any tracked file in this repo matches, the
# push is refused. Put a distinctive string from each sensitive note here, and
# a phrase you would never write in a blog post.
#
# The real `.canary` is NOT committed — a canary living in the repo it guards
# is testing itself. Because of that, this half of the guard is local only;
# the path checks in guard_repo.sh run in CI too.

# A token you paste into your most sensitive notes, e.g. in Finances/:
# CANARY-DO-NOT-PUBLISH-8f2a1c

# Phrases that should never appear on a public site:
# Option Exercise
# strike price
# [0-9]{3}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{4}
